# SCSS Styles Only

All new and updated styles must be written in **SCSS** (`.scss`). Do not add or edit plain CSS, Sass indented (`.sass`), Less, Stylus, or other stylesheet formats.

## Rules

- Put styles in `resources/sass/` (components, layout, page, settings, admin, profile — match existing structure).
- Prefer partials (`_name.scss`) and `@import` them from the relevant entry (usually `resources/sass/app.scss`) when a new file is needed.
- Reuse existing variables, breakpoints, colors, and helpers from `resources/sass/settings/` instead of hardcoding values.
- Do not create or expand `resources/css/*.css`, standalone `.css` assets, or inline large style blocks when an SCSS partial fits.
- Avoid dumping style rules into Blade/`<style>` tags except tiny one-off exceptions that cannot live in SCSS; prefer SCSS by default.
- Do not introduce a parallel CSS pipeline; follow the existing Vite/Laravel Mix SCSS build.

```scss
// ❌ BAD — new plain CSS file
// resources/css/my-feature.css
.my-feature { color: #333; }

// ✅ GOOD — SCSS partial + import from app.scss (or the right entry)
// resources/sass/components/_my-feature.scss
.my-feature {
  color: $text-color;
}
```
